# Anchored covariance identity for the full Schur residual

STATUS: DRAFT_ANALYTIC_IDENTITY; independent review pending.
SCOPE: isolated paper derivation only; no sign advance or canonical admission.
SOURCE_BASE: f6231d59eec72ba78a397dd2c73d205df34dc2c8.
INPUTS: docs/Codex/REPORT_2026-09-14_FULL_V_RANK_TWO_INTAKE.md R2,R7,R15;
docs/Codex/REPORT_2026-09-14_SCHUR_REPEATABILITY.md S1,S2,S14--S16.
OWNER_STEERING: 2026-09-14: pure mathematics and analytical agreement first,
only afterwards numerical tests and formalization. No numerical tests used.

## 1. Same source and domain

Keep the full even positive theta source f=Phi/||Phi||_2 and
V(x,y)=integral_0^infinity (2t+x+y) f(t+x)f(t+y)dt.
All finite node families and all complex coefficients remain required.
The original interval is I=(-log(2)/2,0). R2 proves
V(-x,-y)=V(x,y): simultaneously reflecting every node is a congruent
identical matrix. We may therefore use J=(0,log(2)/2). Choose an anchor a in J.
Write D_a=V(a,a)>0 and S_a(x,y)=V(x,y)-V(x,a)V(a,y)/D_a.

## 2. One positive probability measure, defined before any sign assumption

For t>=0 set
  dmu_a(t) = 2(t+a) f(t+a)^2 dt / D_a,
  r_x(t) = f(t+x)/f(t+a),
  h_a(t) = 1/[2(t+a)],
  A_x(t) = [1+(x-a)h_a(t)]r_x(t),
  B_x(t) = (x-a)h_a(t)r_x(t).

This measure is positive and has total mass one. The definitions use only
the source and one positive diagonal. They require no positivity of a
multi-node matrix, no square root of V, and no new normalization of f.
All A_x,B_x belong to L2(mu_a): h_a<=1/(2a), and the ratios cancel in
integral r_x^2 dmu_a = D_a^(-1) integral 2(t+a)f(t+x)^2 dt < infinity.
Finite linear combinations and cross-products are therefore integrable.

## 3. Exact pairwise identity

Expanding the factors, with delta_x=x-a, gives
  A_x A_y - B_x B_y = r_x r_y [1+(delta_x+delta_y)h_a].
Multiplying by D_a dmu_a recovers precisely
  (2t+x+y)f(t+x)f(t+y)dt.
Thus
  V(x,y)/D_a = E_mu[A_x A_y] - E_mu[B_x B_y].               (A1)

Since A_a=1 and B_a=0,
  E_mu[A_x] = V(x,a)/D_a.
Subtracting the anchor product yields
  S_a(x,y)/D_a =
      E_mu[(A_x-E_mu A_x)(A_y-E_mu A_y)]-E_mu[B_x B_y].     (A2)

For any finite complex coefficient row c let A_c=sum c_i A_(x_i),
B_c=sum c_i B_(x_i). The full exact identity is
  sum conjugate(c_i)S_a(x_i,x_j)c_j / D_a
      = E_mu|A_c-E_mu A_c|^2 - E_mu|B_c|^2.                (A3)

Complex coefficients, all mixed terms, and the whole half-line integral
are retained. No differentiation or integration by parts is used, so no
boundary term is discarded. At the anchor both features in A2 vanish.

## 4. Paid statement versus missing source inequality

R7 already gives, for each individual x!=a,
  E_mu|A_x-E_mu A_x|^2 > E_mu|B_x|^2.
For arbitrary combinations the first unpaid inequality is exactly
  E_mu|B_c|^2 <= E_mu|A_c-E_mu A_c|^2 for every finite c.   (A4)

A4 is equivalent to positivity of the full S_a. Since D_a>0, completing
the anchor square makes A4 for all finite families equivalent to full V
positivity on J (and hence on I). A4 is not proved here. In particular the
individual inequalities do not imply A4 for combinations.

This entrance does not assume positivity of C_V=d_x d_y log V or infinite
divisibility. It is an exact weaker target than that sufficient entrance,
not a new proof or a simplification of the unknown sign by notation alone.

The same identity holds for the non-theta control
f0(u)=exp(-u^2)-exp(-2u^2)/4. Its known negative finite V row prevents A4
from holding for all rows (append anchor and complete the square).
Thus evenness, positivity, tails and squared-coordinate strict log-concavity
alone cannot supply A4. Any successful proof must use additional structure
of the actual theta source. Claiming a contraction that maps centered A_x
to B_x would merely restate A4 unless constructed independently.


## 5. A positive definite comparison form at every finite size

For the ACTUAL full theta source the centered covariance form in A3 is
strictly positive on every nonzero row at distinct nodes x_i in J excluding a.

Proof. The full source series gives, as u tends to positive infinity,
  f(u)=(4pi^2/A) exp(9u/2) exp(-pi exp(2u)) [1-d exp(-2u)+E(exp(2u))],
  d=3/(2pi),
  E(z)=sum_(n>=2) (n^4-d n^2/z) exp[-pi(n^2-1)z].
For z>=1, factoring exp(-3pi z) bounds the remaining series by a
convergent polynomial-weighted Gaussian sum, uniformly in z.
Thus E(z)=O(exp(-3pi z)); this is a bound on the FULL series remainder.

For any fixed x<y in J,
  f(t+y)/f(t+x)
    = exp[9(y-x)/2 - pi(exp(2y)-exp(2x))exp(2t)] (1+o(1))
    -> 0.
The prefactor [1+(y-a)/(2(t+a))]/[1+(x-a)/(2(t+a))] tends to one.
Therefore A_y(t)/A_x(t)->0 whenever x<y. All A_x(t)>0 and A_a=1.

If a finite sum of centered features has zero L2(mu_a) norm, then
sum c_i A_(x_i) is constant mu_a-almost everywhere. The density is strictly
positive on t>=0 and the features are continuous, so the equality holds
everywhere. Adjoin A_a=1 with the negative of that constant as coefficient.
Order the resulting distinct nodes increasingly. Divide the identity by
the feature of the smallest node and let t->infinity: its coefficient is
zero. Repeating finitely many times kills every coefficient. Hence
  E_mu|sum c_i(A_(x_i)-E_mu A_(x_i))|^2 > 0
for every nonzero c, at every finite number of distinct non-anchor nodes.

This pays positive definiteness of the COMPARISON covariance matrix only.
The full difference in A3 still has unknown sign. No quantitative lower
bound uniform in node count, spacing, or coefficients is obtained.

## 6. Decision

RETAIN the exact common-measure accounting A1--A3 and the original target A4.
DO NOT count it as source-sign progress, close a proof node, infer a numerical
witness, replace the source, or dispatch a generic 'prove A4' request.
The source-specific analytical task remains deriving the mixed-term budget
from theta heat/Poisson structure. This note supplies explicit features for
that task; it does not pay that budget or justify a numerical campaign.

AUTOPSY: dropped=COUPLING; note=Exact anchored covariance accounting retains the unpaid all-row budget; no actual-theta source sign is proved.
